# Example music.conf - optional.
#
# zxmusic finds the tunes in its tunes folder by itself and gives each one
# a keyword (shown in MUSIC's browser). This file is only for keywords of
# your own and for options. Copy it to music.conf, next to zxmusic.py.
#
# One KEYWORD=file per line, '#' starts a comment. Paths are relative to
# this file. Keywords are matched case-insensitively: LOAD "MUSIC:TUNE1".
# A keyword can be up to 27 characters (all that LOAD "MUSIC:..." can carry);
# a longer one is skipped with a note in the server log.
# FILE@2 = song 2 of a file with several.
#
# Options, after a '|'; they apply however the tune is picked:
#   scc=3     MSX VGM: put SCC voice 3 on the free AY channel (scc=off: AY only)
#   ts=2      TurboSound PT3: play the second module
#   drums=off sampled drums muted (drums=env: softer AY drums)
#
# Tunes belong to their composers: keep them in tunes/ (not committed).

#COMMANDO=tunes/Project AY_Spectrum_Demos_Commando.ay
#BIONIC3=tunes/bioniccommando.ay@3
#JUNGLE=tunes/msx-tune.vgz | scc=3
#SURFING2=tunes/turbosound.pt3 | ts=2
